# Build context filter for Nami.
#
# Keep the context to source code only: the image has zero runtime
# dependencies, so nothing here is ever needed inside the container.

# --- Dependencies and caches (dev-only tooling; never shipped) ---
node_modules
**/node_modules
.npm-cache
.npm
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Runtime state: databases and logs must never be baked into an image ---
data
**/data
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
*.log
logs

# --- Secrets: real configuration stays on the host ---
# `.env.*` deliberately also excludes `.env.example`, so the image ships code
# only and never a configuration template.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- Version control, editors, OS cruft ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Documentation and local dev config ---
*.md
.npmrc
tsconfig.json

# --- WebUI build toolchain ---
# The compiled WebUI is committed to src/web/app and arrives with `COPY src/`,
# so the image never needs the Vue/Vite toolchain, its node_modules, or its
# sources.
webui
